@meta
id: 23-16
title: Fix the indentation, not the lines
chapter: 23
type: lesson
skills: indent-equals
par: 44
minutes: 5
vscode: select the block, Format Selection
open: order.provider.ts

@brief
Someone pasted the body of `cancel` in from a chat window and every
line landed at a different column. Separately, the `return order;` in
`findOne` has drifted six spaces to the right.

Put every line back at the indentation the formatter would give it.
Not one character of the code itself changes, and nothing outside
those two places is touched — in particular, `ship` is already correct
and must stay byte for byte as it is.

You know `>>` and `<<`. Do not use them; this is not a shift, it is a
re-indent, and vim has an operator that knows where each line belongs.

@keys
| `=={motion}` | re-indent the lines the motion covers |
| `==` | re-indent the current line |
| `=i{` | re-indent everything inside the enclosing braces |
| `=ip` | re-indent the paragraph |
| `gg=G` | re-indent the whole file |

@hints
`/return order` finds the drifted line. `==` puts it where it belongs,
without you saying where.
--
For `cancel`, put the cursor on any line inside the method body that
is not inside a nested block — the `const` line just under the
signature will do — and re-indent inside the braces.
--
`/async cancel` then `j` then `=i{`.

@solution
    /return order<Enter> ==
    /async cancel<Enter> j =i{
    :wq<Enter>

Thirty-eight keystrokes.

`=` is an operator, so it takes the same motions and text objects as
`d` and `y`, and `==` is the line form like `dd`. It asks the
filetype's indent script — `filetype indent on` is set for you — where
each line should sit, and moves it there. It never touches the text
after the indentation, which is why it is safe to run over code you
did not write.

`=i{` is the one to remember. From inside a method body it re-indents
the whole body, nested blocks included, and leaves the signature and
closing brace alone. `=ip` is the same for a paragraph in a file with
no braces to hang on. `gg=G` is the whole file, and is what you do
after a paste has gone wrong somewhere you cannot see; the next
lesson drills it.

The limit is worth knowing: `=` fixes indentation and nothing else. A
line with a missing semicolon or a badly placed brace stays that way,
and an indent script can only be as right as the braces around it. If
`=` puts something somewhere strange, the syntax above it is broken.

@start order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

          return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
const order = await this.findOne(id);

if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
}

        const days = (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

            if (days <= 30) {
      await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
              }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
where: { id },
    values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
  });
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }
}

@expected order.provider.ts
import { injectable, inject } from 'tsyringe';
import { exception } from '../../configuration/errors';
import { OrderRepository } from './order.repository';
import { PaymentService } from '../../infrastructure/services/payment.service';

@injectable()
export class OrderProvider {
  constructor(
    @inject(OrderRepository) protected orderRepository: OrderRepository,
    @inject(PaymentService) protected paymentService: PaymentService,
  ) {}

  public async findOne(id: string) {
    const order = await this.orderRepository.findOne({ where: { id } });

    if (!order) {
      throw exception('ORDER_NOT_FOUND');
    }

    return order;
  }

  public async cancel(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    if (order.status === 'SHIPPED') {
      throw exception('ORDER_ALREADY_SHIPPED');
    }

    const days = (Date.now() - order.placedAt.getTime()) / 86_400_000;

    if (days <= 30) {
      await this.paymentService.refund(order.id);
    }

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'CANCELLED' },
    });
  }

  public async ship(id: string) {
    const order = await this.findOne(id);

    return this.orderRepository.update({
      where: { id },
      values: { status: 'SHIPPED' },
    });
  }
}
